// # sec/cap/zig — Phase 4 deferred to RFC
//
// Logline: This directory is reserved for Phase 4 of the 2026-09-11
//          memory-safety plan (the cap-system rewrite in a memory-
//          safe language). It currently holds only this ANCHOR.oo;
//          the actual implementation lives at sec/cap/cap_check_zig
//          _fallback.c, a C-only TU that provides the same leaf
//          bit-check function the planned Zig module would have.
//
// Setup:  2026-09-11: a previous commit landed three .zig files
//         here (build.zig, cap_check.zig, cap_check_test.zig) as a
//         Phase 4 sample. This violated RULES §1.14 (file law
//         restricts source code to .oo; .zig has no carve-out) and
//         §1.23 (oodar/* is "Layer 1 C shims and Landlock sandbox"
//         — explicitly C only). Those files have been deleted. The
//         same leaf logic is now in sec/cap/cap_check_zig_fallback.c
//         in plain C.
//
//         Full Phase 4 migration (rewriting cap.c, cap_grant.c,
//         cap_alloc.c, cap_attenuate_path.c, cap_attenuate_hmac.c,
//         cap_ffi.c in a memory-safe language) requires an RFC
//         that adds a new file-extension carve-out to RULES §1.14.
//         Without the RFC, no .zig / .rs / .go / .py file may
//         land in this tree. Per §1.14: "add new categories by
//         RFC, not analogy."
//
// Beats:
//   1. The leaf bit-check lives in sec/cap/cap_check_zig_fallback.c.
//   2. Tests for the leaf bit-check live in qa/tests_challenger_cap_
//      check_bits.c (planned; not yet landed).
//   3. Full cap-system migration is deferred to the future RFC.
